-arch/mission-control/commit/301ee9cdd8ba71dabc19ef9ba99587ee6a5c629f","sha":"301ee9cdd8ba71dabc19ef9ba99587ee6a5c629f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/selva-arch/mission-control/commits/301ee9cdd8ba71dabc19ef9ba99587ee6a5c629f"}],"sha":"d87307a4f8764248f818add539b5c30db7701d68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/selva-arch/mission-control/commits/d87307a4f8764248f818add539b5c30db7701d68"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/264638470?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/HonzysClawdbot","id":264638470,"login":"HonzysClawdbot","node_id":"U_kgDOD8YQBg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/selva-arch/mission-control/commits/301ee9cdd8ba71dabc19ef9ba99587ee6a5c629f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-16T04:55:56Z","email":"janclawdbotstratil@gmail.com","name":"HonzysClawdbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-16T04:55:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(gateway): probe /api/health instead of root URL (#394)\n\n* fix(gateway): probe /api/health instead of root URL for health checks (#390)\n\nThe server-side gateway health probe was fetching the root URL (/)\nwhich returns HTTP 400 on OpenClaw 2026.3.13 gateways. The gateway\nexposes a dedicated /api/health endpoint that returns 200 with status\ninfo.\n\nThe WebSocket ping RPC ''unknown method'' issue is already handled —\nwebsocket.ts detects the INVALID_REQUEST and falls back to passive\nheartbeat mode. The actual bug was this HTTP probe hitting the wrong\nendpoint.\n\nFixes #390\n\n* fix(gateway): ensure gateways table exists before health probe\n\nThe gateways table is created lazily by the gateways API (ensureTable).\nThe health route was querying it directly without CREATE IF NOT EXISTS,\ncausing SqliteError: no such table: gateways in fresh databases (E2E tests,\nDocker first-boot).\n\nAdd ensureGatewaysTable() inline to mirror the pattern in route.ts.\n\n* fix: update health-utils test to match /api/health probe path\n\nThe test file has its own copy of buildGatewayProbeUrl — update it to\nappend /api/health instead of / to match the route.ts change.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nyk <0xnykcd@googlemail.com>","tree":{"sha":"fb8d578986aed377e33786c5b7bf8fb355941e87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/selva-arch/mission-control/git/trees/fb8d578986aed377e33786c5b7bf8fb355941e87"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/selva-arch/mission-control/git/commits/301ee9cdd8ba71dabc19ef9ba99587ee6a5c629f","verification":{"payload":"tree fb8d578986aed377e33786c5b7bf8fb355941e87\nparent 0acf7daf320dd7b0a4e1dbbe506af7a4ad0cdeac\nauthor HonzysClawdbot <janclawdbotstratil@gmail.com> 1773636956 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773636956 +0700\n\nfix(gateway): probe /api/health instead of root URL (#394)\n\n* fix(gateway): probe /api/health instead of root URL for health checks (#390)\n\nThe server-side gateway health probe was fetching the root URL (/)\nwhich returns HTTP 400 on OpenClaw 2026.3.13 gateways. The gateway\nexposes a dedicated /api/health endpoint that returns 200 with status\ninfo.\n\nThe WebSocket ping RPC ''unknown method'' issue is already handled —\nwebsocket.ts detects the INVALID_REQUEST and falls back to passive\nheartbeat mode. The actual bug was this HTTP probe hitting the wrong\nendpoint.\n\nFixes #390\n\n* fix(gateway): ensure gateways table exists before health probe\n\nThe gateways table is created lazily by the gateways API (ensureTable).\nThe health route was querying it directly without CREATE IF NOT EXISTS,\ncausing SqliteError: no such table: gateways in fresh databases (E2E tests,\nDocker first-boot).\n\nAdd ensureGatewaysTable() inline to mirror the pattern in route.ts.\n\n* fix: update health-utils test to match /api/health probe path\n\nThe test file has its own copy of buildGatewayProbeUrl — update it to\nappend /api/health instead of / to match the route.ts change.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nyk <0xnykcd@googlemail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpt41cCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAue4QAFMFqjWr/gxXn+tnm0PvmLL1\nPfGsDgk3GXpjhpeavKERz87WqSLwUy5b8YnUnHQ2wAqWWeUXj36lRHPpP+4irOP5\njPuw9b0WbJI5UrZS0ZQkTDon8n41ABv6becHr+YZWxUQ4eK20VaIecBd8wNIvw8K\n7xG6/OSQsvg/dNNiT/EBykywC99rD1fYm/m3C+xcy6haWUF3Jwetp1z2g6zNNy7N\nJIvpU+CtTJPeBfiF7qrFsUrD8302Ng3slgh0hMu30ASn1WY9KrpXIPZXfWuDpSGz\nS2gt+QIijR2/tJW8l51inoOoLuWzFAoCIwTkPsMOm9RErAwNfZF6nXHuWNvqSZvt\nKUfVDVtRhYZyLUPpWttcd0Ho0i8OdizeCl10LEzXcSht2No9wDyPYYBoU17ysnv9\nvOa0PfQSlmuSwHCf+fsQZyDrjiC4r+USXavxxrQ55ZgdfQzsXfUw8pO9nSWLLWAT\n1kVFOT/Lj/qzNYDDfm+ZRT0FHnJNRB9kNZtNbJzrNHdcHUoH3z+Wg0pdgykBK0kK\ndqwtbajAq7wgJOk43Ix85VtBiOMQseTdEH01thEaDvgw0mlw4MwlI97xz5pSTpnp\nXlE/2BX0sZ/H0Shl7UykV4u3QC42AzKNZDCr+nU2kGBFbR+X8nA97VrpoEz7rWyd\nYfoEerkvi0Bedx3rC5Vo\n=qX73\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-28T03:14:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/selva-arch/mission-control/commit/301ee9cdd8ba71dabc19ef9ba99587ee6a5c629f","node_id":"C_kwDORy4A5toAKDMwMWVlOWNkZDhiYTcxZGFiYzE5ZWY5YmE5OTU4N2VlNmE1YzYyOWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/selva-arch/mission-control/commit/0acf7daf320dd7b0a4e1dbbe506af7a4ad0cdeac","sha":"0acf7daf320dd7b0a4e1dbbe506af7a4ad0cdeac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/selva-arch/mission-control/commits/0acf7daf320dd7b0a4e1dbbe506af7a4ad0cdeac"}],"sha":"301ee9cdd8ba71dabc19ef9ba99587ee6a5c629f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/selva-arch/mission-control/commits/301ee9cdd8ba71dabc19ef9ba99587ee6a5c629f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/264638470?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/HonzysClawdbot","id":264638470,"login":"HonzysClawdbot","node_id":"U_kgDOD8YQBg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HonzysClawdbot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/selva-arch/mission-control/commits/0acf7daf320dd7b0a4e1dbbe506af7a4ad0cdeac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-16T04:34:28Z","email":"janclawdbotstratil@gmail.com","name":"HonzysClawdbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-16T04:34:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: task assignment session targeting (#399)\n\n* feat: add task session targeting - dispatch tasks to specific agent sessions (#395)\n\nWhen assigning a task to an agent, users can now optionally select an\nexisting session to dispatch the task to instead of creating a new one.\n\nChanges:\n- task-dispatch.ts: When target_session is set in task metadata, use\n  gateway chat.send to dispatch to that specific session instead of\n  creating a new one via call agent\n- task-board-panel.tsx: Add session selector dropdown in both Create\n  and Edit task modals that appears when an agent is selected and has\n  active sessions\n- store/index.ts: Add agent and channel fields to Session interface\n\nCloses #395\n\n* fix(gateway): ensure gateways table exists before health probe\n\nThe gateways table is created lazily by the gateways API (ensureTable).\nThe health route was querying it directly without CREATE IF NOT EXISTS,\ncausing SqliteError: no such table: gateways in fresh databases (E2E tests,\nDocker first-boot).\n\nAdd ensureGatewaysTable() inline to mirror the pattern in route.ts.","tree":{"sha":"4d8bc162ed0bf6a7d607b4083c538e2fac9c470b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/selva-arch/mission-control/git/trees/4d8bc162ed0bf6a7d607b4083c538e2fac9c470b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/selva-arch/mission-control/git/commits/0acf7daf320dd7b0a4e1dbbe506af7a4ad0cdeac","verification":{"payload":"tree 4d8bc162ed0bf6a7d607b4083c538e2fac9c470b\nparent e7aa7e6a917715e52b40f1d5012f1402f6a5209d\nauthor HonzysClawdbot <janclawdbotstratil@gmail.com> 1773635668 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773635668 +0700\n\nfeat: task assignment session targeting (#399)\n\n* feat: add task session targeting - dispatch tasks to specific agent sessions (#395)\n\nWhen assigning a task to an agent, users can now optionally select an\nexisting session to dispatch the task to instead of creating a new one.\n\nChanges:\n- task-dispatch.ts: When target_session is set in task metadata, use\n  gateway chat.send to dispatch to that specific session instead of\n  creating a new one via call agent\n- task-board-panel.tsx: Add session selector dropdown in both Create\n  and Edit task modals that appears when an agent is selected and has\n  active sessions\n- store/index.ts: Add agent and channel fields to Session interface\n\nCloses #395\n\n* fix(gateway): ensure gateways table exists before health probe\n\nThe gateways table is created lazily by the gateways API (ensureTable).\nThe health route was querying it directly without CREATE IF NOT EXISTS,\ncausing SqliteError: no such table: gateways in fresh databases (E2E tests,\nDocker first-boot).\n\nAdd ensureGatewaysTable() inline to mirror the pattern in route.ts.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpt4hUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbDMQAA1aWBa9hgC9K50XOOEAkRjN\n8KJL39AgUdJrf/Fmznx61SKlCH3222f3/rfGPTxYs/UGOc1b344jmqeB0+D0mSuC\n5gkP28oeviz8CVq065a/fpsMW6HPy/FqYVA4dXUjWvIICCxBhLmOE2HcyNCfUGzl\nIuZKyYHSDHcWqdvnsIILGqg7782e3wC8nSfOdaDbBJ7LUVJQr//S2hpYhjiVXotO\nxuXoQu/+SlpLXU+Ui5lpGNhaxo9GKhsgMBTZNiaUCnbpnJbu0c7vsEoQ0UV4uLui\n9hxjpBooMk4V6OB9VVTHi22yRESnAbHVFWZzayfo3rSqd05+n2DXiBNKO6ygSiFW\noX3RCoEVjYHAhvq2Vr0YDAhqVZYuKng9R0/7c5A7AuY/Zpd7Z0nHDJ/BBpT/spFH\nRTKbYQo8MbJw8n8jQYk4yBcdZVUWnpiw4wTkv09pckF/KPWJ5QVzZDVaBqHes8PX\nEbLpeOadbeFw