arred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/signalk-plugin-registry/commit/4e4d7e3ee4e7ec2bb5558079f30bc95119e92218","node_id":"C_kwDORy6_G9oAKDRlNGQ3ZTNlZTRlN2VjMmJiNTU1ODA3OWYzMGJjOTUxMTllOTIyMTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/signalk-plugin-registry/commit/43eafbf394a58bd99434ddf00cefd7696c03832f","sha":"43eafbf394a58bd99434ddf00cefd7696c03832f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-plugin-registry/commits/43eafbf394a58bd99434ddf00cefd7696c03832f"}],"sha":"4e4d7e3ee4e7ec2bb5558079f30bc95119e92218","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-plugin-registry/commits/4e4d7e3ee4e7ec2bb5558079f30bc95119e92218"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-plugin-registry/commits/43eafbf394a58bd99434ddf00cefd7696c03832f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T16:45:27Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T16:45:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: penalize legacy baconjs and React 16 embedded webapps (#81)\n\n* feat: penalize legacy baconjs and React 16 embedded webapps\n\nThe server provides baconjs 3 and a React 19 admin UI, and keeps older\nplugin builds working only through two temporary compatibility shims:\na module-resolution hook that redirects every require(''baconjs'') to the\nserver''s copy (signalk-server#2487) and an isolated ReactDOM.render\nbridge for Module Federation remotes built against React 16\n(signalk-server#2342, #2452, reminder #2451). Both are slated for\nremoval once the ecosystem moves, but nothing pushed plugins to move:\nas of 2026-08-18, 22 published plugins still declare baconjs <3 and 8\nembedded webapps still ship React 16.14.0 - three of them published in\nthe last month.\n\nAdd a legacy runtime-dep check, pure file inspection with no plugin\ncode executed:\n\n- baconjs: a dependencies/peerDependencies range that cannot resolve\n  to any 3.x release (e.g. ^0.7.88, ^1.0.1) - devDependencies never\n  reach user installs; *, >=1, dist-tags, git/URL specs and invalid\n  ranges are skipped.\n- react: for plugins with an embedded-webapp keyword\n  (signalk-embeddable-webapp, signalk-plugin-configurator,\n  signalk-node-server-addon), scan the shipped bundles under public/\n  for the shared React major they register - webpack (\"react\",\"16.14.0\"\n  in both the factory and the curried form newer webpack emits, and\n  vite MF name:`react`,version:`...` - and flag a major below 19. The\n  webpack regex is the admin UI''s own containerUsesLegacyReact()\n  pattern so registry and bridge agree. Consume-only remotes\n  (import: false) register nothing and run on the host''s React.\n\nThe tarball is untrusted, so the bundle walk is bounded: iterative, at\nmost 500 files, depth 8, 16 MiB per file, 64 MiB total, symlinks never\nfollowed; scanning stops at the first legacy hit and anything past a\nlimit is indeterminate, never a penalty.\n\nEach finding costs -15 and adds a legacy-baconjs / legacy-react badge.\nWired through runner, scorer, result envelope, merge validation\n(VALID_BADGES + shape check), plan-runs schema_change backfill, and the\npublished API/HTML/guide. Verified against the 40 tarballs from the\necosystem audit: 22 baconjs + 8 React flagged, all React 19 and\nconsume-only remotes clean.\n\n* fix: scan only what remoteEntry.js can reach, accept 3.x prereleases\n\nSelf-audit of the legacy-dep check against a wider set of real\npackages (70 tarballs, all 45 published embedded webapps included)\nturned up one false positive and a few weaknesses:\n\n- signalk-ais-navionics-converter ships a stale unminified React 16\n  build (public/main.js) next to a consume-only remoteEntry.js. The\n  browser never loads main.js, the admin UI does not bridge the plugin,\n  yet a whole-directory scan flagged it. Replace the recursive walk of\n  public/ with a bounded traversal of remoteEntry.js and the relative\n  .js references reachable from it, resolved relative to the importing\n  file. That is exactly what the admin UI can execute: webpack registers\n  shared versions in the entry, and every @module-federation/vite layout\n  in the wild reaches its localSharedImportMap chunk in one to two hops\n  (signalk-doctor 1.0.1 needs two). Verified: all eight React 16 remotes\n  still flagged, every React 19 vite remote''s registration reached,\n  navionics and the other consume-only remotes clean.\n- A 3.x prerelease pin (3.0.0-beta.1) was flagged because\n  semver.intersects(range, \">=3.0.0\") excludes prereleases; the lower\n  bound is now 3.0.0-0.\n- The webpack and vite patterns tolerate whitespace so an unminified\n  development build is detected too; a matching fixture from navionics''\n  main.js is the new dev-build test case.\n- The scorer applies -15 per library, not per entry, and narrows\n  keywords to strings before matching.\n- Test fixtures are removed after the run.","tree":{"sha":"cee4f7d35b10afe43acf921ee3de1c2fd9eeeb66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-plugin-registry/git/trees/cee4f7d35b10afe43acf921ee3de1c2fd9eeeb66"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/signalk-plugin-registry/git/commits/43eafbf394a58bd99434ddf00cefd7696c03832f","verification":{"payload":"tree cee4f7d35b10afe43acf921ee3de1c2fd9eeeb66\nparent 18f97639616314a45c382615c086a8acf2070dff\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1790527527 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790527527 +0300\n\nfeat: penalize legacy baconjs and React 16 embedded webapps (#81)\n\n* feat: penalize legacy baconjs and React 16 embedded webapps\n\nThe server provides baconjs 3 and a React 19 admin UI, and keeps older\nplugin builds working only through two temporary compatibility shims:\na module-resolution hook that redirects every require(''baconjs'') to the\nserver''s copy (signalk-server#2487) and an isolated ReactDOM.render\nbridge for Module Federation remotes built against React 16\n(signalk-server#2342, #2452, reminder #2451). Both are slated for\nremoval once the ecosystem moves, but nothing pushed plugins to move:\nas of 2026-08-18, 22 published plugins still declare baconjs <3 and 8\nembedded webapps still ship React 16.14.0 - three of them published in\nthe last month.\n\nAdd a legacy runtime-dep check, pure file inspection with no plugin\ncode executed:\n\n- baconjs: a dependencies/peerDependencies range that cannot resolve\n  to any 3.x release (e.g. ^0.7.88, ^1.0.1) - devDependencies never\n  reach user installs; *, >=1, dist-tags, git/URL specs and invalid\n  ranges are skipped.\n- react: for plugins with an embedded-webapp keyword\n  (signalk-embeddable-webapp, signalk-plugin-configurator,\n  signalk-node-server-addon), scan the shipped bundles under public/\n  for the shared React major they register - webpack (\"react\",\"16.14.0\"\n  in both the factory and the curried form newer webpack emits, and\n  vite MF name:`react`,version:`...` - and flag a major below 19. The\n  webpack regex is the admin UI''s own containerUsesLegacyReact()\n  pattern so registry and bridge agree. Consume-only remotes\n  (import: false) register nothing and run on the host''s React.\n\nThe tarball is untrusted, so the bundle walk is bounded: iterative, at\nmost 500 files, depth 8, 16 MiB per file, 64 MiB total, symlinks never\nfollowed; scanning stops at the first legacy hit and anything past a\nlimit is indeterminate, never a penalty.\n\nEach finding costs -15 and adds a legacy-baconjs / legacy-react badge.\nWired through runner, scorer, result envelope, merge validation\n(VALID_BADGES + shape check), plan-runs schema_change backfill, and the\npublished API/HTML/guide. Verified against the 40 tarballs from the\necosystem audit: 22 baconjs + 8 React flagged, all React 19 and\nconsume-only remotes clean.\n\n* fix: scan only what remoteEntry.js can reach, accept 3.x prereleases\n\nSelf-audit of the legacy-dep check against a wider set of real\npackages (70 tarballs, all 45 published embedded webapps included)\nturned up one false positive and a few weaknesses:\n\n- signalk-ais-navionics-converter ships a stale unminified React 16\n  build (public/main.js) next to a consume-only remoteEntry.js. The\n  browser never loads main.js, the admin UI does not bridge the plugin,\n  yet a whole-directory scan flagged it. Replace the recursive walk of\n  public/ with a bounded traversal of remoteEntry.js and the relative\n  .js references reachable from it, resolved relative to the importing\n  file. That is exactly what the admin UI can execute: webpack registers\n  shared versions in the entry, and every @module-federation/vite layout\n  in the wild reaches its localSharedImportMap chunk in one to two hops\n  (signalk-doctor 1.0.1 needs two). Verified: all eight React 16 remotes\n  still flagged, every React 19 vite remote''s registration reached,\n  navionics and the other consume-only remotes clean.\n- A 3.x prerelease pin (3.0.0-beta.1) was flagged because\n  semver.intersects(range, \">=3.0.0\") excludes prereleases; the lower\n  bound is now 3.0.0-0.\n- The webpack and vite patterns tolerate whitespace so an unminified\n  development build is detected too; a matching fixture from navionics''\n  main.js is the new dev-build test case.\n- The scorer applies -15 per library, not per entry, and narrows\n  keywords to strings before matching.\n- Test fixtures are removed after the run.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquUgnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEoQQAEQGDM7UnADzSLzMwZKVXzV2\nJIknUKpUzN7VHJTuDDXgr8xoUlnsaQoC1FQQcEohdSKX22OGrRdAun2a4HuvwJZF\nGsiha+o/dHSx5qIImViWtBCraAXjSWPt/OGqNZliZeFuPhD8sR2pzKndDC9lMLiI\nLONWPYlLacs1h5AZuvqgppKzfTX1dKsSbecKFUHDPmOCgp9OeR6n0bwuUGHlYy2e\nFJDM1uI5mO7Bp+QM9HdiThBUwihmCy0RgI1RRzFJ5cQfDlSXbF/q2ijoEUxa+gAo\nOUS9tm/La11WELpx78ZZgkRlebQWUBeXmzoTyDY5WU9bYJyImy6bw1eV4mkKc0ZX\nRn6FuRixVBJm1oNbZoBJHmkTIVPwFTiWMzqjG6ER0xSxQDH71pLEl7YFE/uGpm9q\nHOeuDEIV6kPkDxq7oe/Tw8USGeuEIo0xX3lnsU0sJRrEF09thJOTO3b9G2QtWJo5\nXOR6anIcIr8ZytJtocoJwRH0Twki2lOQL0PSS042ccSw+z6jS8JTs94a4vXT9Pfl\nmHSxic/ynSNbnhxN+gNVKbHvI4rygwPOYw3oexENFBe8vRiOASXM/JJjaBWfvwwj\nrmnNVUIkp5VjSO2tFyb+fZdjbKmn2rZbkhG40sehm7KCzJvDpIUCezmosZCqADBV\na1vB5SSzs4xa17IettvB\n=dWCn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T16:45:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_